            <ArticleTitle>Paracetamol for injection: new formulation. New formulation: why so widely used?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>178</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paracetamol for injection appears to cause fewer local reactions than propacetamol. However, the added therapeutic value of the parenteral route is not supported by a thorough comparative evaluation. The widespread use of this product in hospitals is worrying</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
